Description: wiki with MoinMoin syntax and Markdown pages (Python 3)
 MoinMoin is a wiki engine written in Python. It supports many markups
 (its own wiki syntax, Creole, reStructuredText, HTML), page history and
 diffs, attachments, access control lists, user accounts, search,
 themes and plugins (actions, macros, parsers, formatters).
 .
 This is MoinMoin 1.12.0 (moinmoin-py3-md): MoinMoin 1.9.11 ported to
 Python 3, with pages written in Markdown next to the pages in MoinMoin
 wiki syntax (recognized from the text, or set with "#format markdown").
 Markdown pages support wiki links, attachments, macros, syntax
 highlighting and blocks in wiki syntax. Existing 1.9 wikis can be used
 without converting the data. The wiki can be run
 with its own web server (an init script for sysvinit is included), with
 any WSGI server (Apache mod_wsgi, uWSGI, gunicorn), as CGI, FastCGI or
 SCGI.
 .
 Not supported in this port: the Jabber notification bot (its pyxmpp
 library only exists for Python 2) and the DocBook/XSLT parsers that
 need 4Suite.
